# esphome-truma_inetbox — Project Overview

ESPHome external component that emulates a Truma iNet box over a LIN bus to remotely control a CP Plus heater.

## Repository layout

```
components/truma_inetbox/   ← the ESPHome component (C++ + Python codegen)
  __init__.py               ← top-level component schema & automation registration
  <platform>/__init__.py    ← per-entity schema (binary_sensor, climate, number, select, sensor, time)
  LinBusListener.*          ← UART/ISR layer; one platform-specific .cpp per framework
  LinBusProtocol.*          ← LIN diagnostic-frame state machine
  TrumaiNetBoxApp.*         ← top-level app, owns sub-apps
  TrumaiNetBoxApp{Heater,Timer,Clock,AirconAuto,AirconManual,Config}.*
  TrumaStructs.h / TrumaEnums.h / helpers.*
tests/                      ← ESPHome compile targets (one per platform×framework)
examples/                   ← user-facing example YAMLs (not CI targets)
*.yaml (root)               ← personal/integration example configs
.github/workflows/main.yml  ← CI: `esphome compile` for every test/*.yaml
.clang-format / .clang-tidy ← enforced C++ style
```

## Three-layer C++ architecture

```
UART ISR  →  LinBusListener  →  LinBusProtocol  →  TrumaiNetBoxApp
                                                     └── sub-apps (Heater, Timer, …)
```

- **LinBusListener** owns UART setup, interrupt/event-task wiring, and raw LIN frame parsing into a FreeRTOS queue. Platform-specific setup lives in `LinBusListener_esp32_arduino.cpp`, `LinBusListener_esp_idf.cpp`, `LinBusListener_rp2040.cpp`.
- **LinBusProtocol** handles LIN transport-layer framing (node address, multi-PDU reassembly, update queue).
- **TrumaiNetBoxApp** implements the Truma application protocol and delegates to sub-apps.

## Supported platforms

| Platform | Framework | Guard macro |
|---|---|---|
| ESP32 | Arduino | `USE_ESP32_FRAMEWORK_ARDUINO` |
| ESP32 | ESP-IDF | `USE_ESP32_FRAMEWORK_ESP_IDF` |
| RP2040 | Arduino | `USE_RP2040` |

Any new platform-diverging code must go into the appropriate `LinBusListener_<platform>.cpp` behind the correct `#ifdef`.
